{
  "verdict": "void",
  "section": "134",
  "quote": "No landlord shall, directly or indirectly, with respect to any rental unit, collect or require or attempt to collect or require from a former tenant of the rental unit any amount of money purporting to be rent in respect of, (a) any period after the tenancy has terminated and the tenant has vacated the rental unit;",
  "reason": "Section 134 prohibits a landlord from requiring or collecting rent from a former tenant for any period after the tenancy has terminated and the tenant has vacated the rental unit. Under section 4, any provision in a tenancy agreement inconsistent with this prohibition is void."
}

